  "instructions": [
    "Combine rye flour, wheat flour, salt, sugar, sourdough starter, yeast in a mixing bowl.",
    "Gradually add water while mixing until a shaggy dough forms.",
    "Knead the dough for 10 minutes until smooth.",
    "Place the dough in a lightly oiled bowl, cover with plastic wrap, and let rise in a warm place for 1 hour.",
    "Preheat the oil in a deep frying pan to 180°C.",
    "Punch down the dough and divide into 4 equal pieces.",
    "Roll out each piece into a thin circle.",
    "Deep-fry the flatbreads for 2-3 minutes on each side, until golden brown.",
    "Drain the flatbreads on paper towels.",
    "Brush the flatbreads with olive oil, sprinkle with chopped fresh dill, black pepper, caraway seeds, sesame seeds, grated onion, garlic, and fennel seeds.",
    "Serve the Polish Rye Bread Flatbread hot or at room temperature."
